### Managing Exceptions  inHerited classes
Some rule are There
Rule:- 
1. If Parent class Methods, is throwing an Exception, then Child Class Overrridden method might not throw Exception
public class Parent {
	void display() throws Exception
	{
		System.out.println("Inside parent disp");
	}
}
public class Child extends Parent {
	@Override
	void display()
	{
		System.out.println("insside child disp");
	}
}
public class Main {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Child ch = new Child();
		ch.display();
	}
}

Rule 2:- If Parent class Methods, is throwing an Exception, then Child Class Overrridden method also throw Exception
public class Parent {
	void display() throws Exception
	{
		System.out.println("Inside parent disp");
	}
}
public class Child extends Parent {
	@Override
	void display() throws Exception
	{
		System.out.println("insside child disp");
	}
}
public class Main1 {
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		Child ch = new Child();
		try {
			ch.display();
		} catch (Exception e) {
			e.printStackTrace();
		}
	}
}

